### Setup

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone {{.ModuleName}}
cd {{.ProjectName}}

# Copy environment variables
cp .env.example .env

# Generate an RS256 keypair and add the base64-encoded PEMs to .env.
# Only the token-issuing service needs JWT_PRIVATE_KEY; verify-only services
# set JWT_PUBLIC_KEY alone.
openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -pkeyopt rsa_keygen_bits:2048 -out jwt.key
openssl rsa -in jwt.key -pubout -out jwt.pub
sed -i.bak "s|^JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=.*|JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=$(base64 < jwt.pub | tr -d '\n')|" .env
sed -i.bak "s|^JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=.*|JWT_PRIVATE_KEY=$(base64 < jwt.key | tr -d '\n')|" .env && rm .env.bak

# Install dependencies{{if or .UseWire (eq .QueryGen "sqlc") .HasGRPC}} + run code generators ({{if .UseWire}}wire{{if or (eq .QueryGen "sqlc") .HasGRPC}}, {{end}}{{end}}{{if eq .QueryGen "sqlc"}}sqlc{{if .HasGRPC}}, {{end}}{{end}}{{if .HasGRPC}}proto{{end}}){{end}}
go mod tidy{{if or .UseWire (eq .QueryGen "sqlc") .HasGRPC}}
make gen{{end}}
{{- if .IncludeDocker}}

# Start infrastructure (database, cache, etc.)
docker-compose up -d
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasDatabase}}

# Run migrations
make migrate-up
{{- end}}

# Run the server
{{- if .HasWorker}}
go run main.go worker
{{- else}}
go run main.go api
{{- end}}
```

{{- if .HasWorker}}

### Worker process

This binary subscribes to a message broker ({{.MessageQueue}}) and processes
events emitted by an upstream publisher (e.g. a sibling project generated
with `nova new --transport=http --queue={{.MessageQueue}}`). The current
handler set:

| Topic            | Handler                                        | Side effect                            |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `user.created`   | `transport/worker/v1/user.Handler.Handle`      | Inserts a row into `user_audit_log`    |

End-to-end demo:

1. Start {{.MessageQueue}} and {{if eq .Database "postgres"}}Postgres{{else}}MySQL{{end}} locally (docker-compose recommended).
2. `make migrate-up` — creates `users` and `user_audit_log`.
3. Generate the publisher counterpart in another directory:
   `nova new {{.ProjectName}}-api --transport=http --http-framework=fiber --database={{.Database}} --queue={{.MessageQueue}}`.
4. Run the publisher (`go run main.go api`) and the worker (`go run main.go worker`).
5. `curl -X POST localhost:8080/api/v1/users -d '{"email":"a@b","name":"A","password":"hunter2-pass"}'`.
6. `SELECT * FROM user_audit_log;` — see the inbound `user.created` row.
{{- end}}

